4. Master Speech
One of the largest programs I led was the Product Feature Store modernisation. The organisation needed to migrate a large Oracle-based platform supporting forecasting, replenishment and machine learning workloads into Azure Databricks.
I led the solution end-to-end, including architecture, framework design, migration planning, validation strategy and deployment.
One of the key design decisions was building a reusable metadata-driven framework that supported both historical rebuilds and incremental processing through a single codebase.
One of the biggest technical challenges was validating data equivalence between Oracle and Databricks. We encountered differences in aggregation behaviour, token ordering and calculation logic. To address this, I built automated reconciliation and regression frameworks that provided confidence before production deployment.
I worked closely with Data Scientists, Business SMEs, Platform Teams and Enterprise Architects throughout the migration.
The result was a scalable, governed and reliable cloud platform that improved maintainability, accelerated future feature development and became the foundation for multiple downstream machine learning initiatives.
