4. Master Speech
One initiative I'm particularly proud of was improving the Range Optimisation platform.
The platform was experiencing performance and cost issues, and rather than scaling infrastructure, I focused on understanding the root cause.
Through end-to-end analysis, I discovered that significant transformation logic was repeatedly being executed inside the R application layer.
This created unnecessary processing overhead and increased operational cost.
I redesigned the architecture by moving heavy transformations into Databricks, persisting reusable Delta datasets and optimising the SQL processing layer.
I also migrated the workload to a right-sized Serverless SQL Warehouse.
The result was approximately 30% performance improvement and about 15% reduction in compute costs.
The key lesson was that architecture improvements often deliver greater value than infrastructure scaling.
