4. Master Speech
One of the biggest challenges I face is source data discovery within a large and complex enterprise landscape.
Data Scientists often require new features, but those features rarely exist in a single source system. Information such as promotions, pricing, inventory, sales and range data often originates from different systems with multiple integration layers in between.
My approach begins with Business SMEs to understand the business process, business rules and user behaviour.
Next, I work with source-system architects and IT teams to understand tables, interfaces, ownership and application-level implementation.
I then engage Enterprise Architects to understand lineage and how data moves across the organisation because some datasets travel through four or five different systems before reaching the analytics platform.
Once I understand the business process, technical implementation and data behaviour, I design the acquisition approach, onboard the data into Databricks and build machine-learning-ready datasets.
I describe myself as the one-stop front for Data Scientists because I own everything from discovery through delivery.
The biggest lesson is that understanding the business process is often more important than understanding the technology.
